-- title:
--   Period group of a differential basis has ≤ 2n generators
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, and assume there is a transcendental element $x \in F$ over $\mathbb{C}$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ obtained by adjoining $x$. Assume `IsCurveOver ℂ F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor of degree $0$ whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$, each residue field of a place is finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega[F⁄\mathbb{C}]$ is free of rank one over $F$; and assume `HasCanonicalDivisor`, i.e. every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega[F⁄\mathbb{C}]$ has a divisor whose value at each $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}(\omega) = v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the coefficient of $\omega$ against $v.\mathrm{dCoord} = D(v.\mathrm{uniformizer})$. Assume further that the set of places $\mathrm{Place}(\mathbb{C}, F)$ carries a topology, charts modelled on $\mathbb{C}$ making it an analytic manifold for the model $\mathcal{I}(\mathbb{C},\mathbb{C})$, and is compact, Hausdorff and connected, and that (hypothesis `hF`) for every nonzero $f \in F$ and every place $v$ the function $z \mapsto \mathrm{evalAt}$ of $f$ at the point of the chart inverse at $z$ is meromorphic at the chart image of $v$ with meromorphic order there equal to $v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$. Finally let $b$ be a basis of the $\mathbb{C}$-vector space of regular differentials — those $\omega$ that at each place $v$ can be written $f \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$ with $f$ in the valuation ring of $v$ — indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$. Then there is a finite subset $s$ of $\mathbb{C}^n = (\mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathbb{C})$ with at most $2n$ elements whose $\mathbb{Z}$-span is exactly `pathPeriodLattice` of the underlying differentials $b_i$, that is, the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{C}^n$ spanned by all vectors $\bigl(\mathrm{pathIntegral}(b_i, \gamma)\bigr)_i$ for a place $P$ and a loop $\gamma$ at $P$, where $\mathrm{pathIntegral}(\omega, \gamma)$ is $g(1) - g(0)$ for a primitive $g$ of $\omega$ along $\gamma$ when one exists and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the finiteness half of the assertion that the period group of a basis of holomorphic differentials on a compact Riemann surface is a full lattice in $\mathbb{C}^n$: classically the period homomorphism factors through $H_1$ of the surface, which for a compact orientable surface of genus $g$ is generated by $2g$ classes. It is used, together with the statement that the real span of the period group is everything, in [`AlgebraicCurve.discreteTopology_pathPeriodLattice_and_span_eq_top`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.discreteTopology_pathPeriodLattice_and_span_eq_top), on the way to the Abel–Jacobi description of principal divisors.
